{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210737,"nonce":"y2bW5UWK8lNfSRdXNPz/iXrV1mw=","title":"Tiered JIT mis-dispatched Stylesheet.add's _styles.add to Request.style","message":"Closed 2026-09-12: no longer reproduces at 5792bac (interpreter and tiered). Fixing commit not identified; repro kept below in case it regresses.\n\n\n```\n$ wlift hatch/packages/hatch-web/examples/styled.wren\n@hatch:web listening on http://127.0.0.1:3000\nRuntime error: Right operand must be a string.\nError: type guard failed: expected num\n     ╭─[ \u003cunknown\u003e:624:17 ]        \u003c- css.wren, `static sheet { Stylesheet.new() }`\n     at add(_) (./css)\n     at style(_) (../web)\n     at add(_) (./css)             \u003c- recursive Stylesheet.add\n     at style(_) (../web)          \u003c- mis-dispatch to Request.style\n     at add(_) (./css)\n     at style(_) (../web)\n     ...\nzsh: bus error\n```\n\nInterpreter mode (`--mode interpreter`) runs the same program cleanly.\n\n\n`req.style(card)` calls `fragmentSheet.add(card)`. Inside Stylesheet.add:\n\n```wren\nadd(style) {\n  var name = style.className\n  if (!_seen.containsKey(name)) {\n    _seen[name] = true\n    _styles.add(style)            \u003c- List.add\n  }\n  return style\n}\n```\n\nThe `_styles.add(style)` should dispatch to `List.add(_)` because `_styles` is a List. The tiered JIT's inline cache — populated from the method-lookup for an earlier, structurally-similar call — instead routes the dispatch to `Request.style(_)` (which itself calls `fragmentSheet.add`, hence the recursion).\n\nThe type-guard error on `Css.sheet` is a downstream artefact: once the method IC is poisoned, downstream bytecode executes with bogus operands and the first type guard that fires (here, the `num` guard on the Stylesheet constructor's return) is what gets reported.\n\n\n- Reproduces only in tiered mode. `--mode interpreter` works.\n- Reproduces across runs (deterministic).\n- Minimal Stylesheet + List.add doesn't repro (`/tmp/rep.wren` passes).\n  Needs the @hatch:web file layout and cross-module context to trigger.\n- `WLIFT_SKIP_JIT=add,style,className` doesn't help — the mis-\n  dispatch happens earlier in the call chain.\n\n\n- Method-IC misses under cross-module class collisions. Even\n  though the `find_imported_var` fix ensures module vars point\n  at the right class, the JIT's method-lookup IC (populated by\n  Phase 1 interpretation) might cache a pointer from a shadowed\n  import — a ghost of the old bug.\n- Receiver-type specialization confusion when `_styles` (List)\n  and `this` (Stylesheet) are both objects of similar shape at\n  the IC site.\n\n\n1. Run with `WLIFT_JIT_DEBUG=1 WLIFT_JIT_DUMP=1` and inspect the\n   MIR + IR for Stylesheet.add — confirm whether the emitted\n   direct call goes to List.add or Request.style.\n2. Dump `engine.type_profiles` for the Stylesheet.add FuncId\n   and see whether the JIT specialized on a stale receiver class.\n3. Try `WLIFT_DISABLE_JIT_CALLSITE_IC=1` (if that flag exists)\n   to confirm the IC is the source.\n\n\n`wlift --mode interpreter examples/styled.wren` until fixed.\nThe example's header comment carries this note.","files":null}]}